    "Stem": "Bramblewood Manufacturing's Q3 flexible budget report shows an $87,000 favorable total flexible budget variance ($1,243,000 actual costs vs. $1,330,000 flexible budget at 52,000 actual units). The Controller decomposes this into three components: (1) Direct materials: $42,000 favorable — the purchasing manager attributes this to negotiating a 7% price reduction with a new supplier; (2) Direct labor: $28,000 unfavorable — the production manager reports that the new supplier's material required additional machining time, adding 0.3 hours per unit at $18/hour across 52,000 units; (3) Variable overhead: $73,000 favorable — the maintenance supervisor reports that preventive maintenance spending came in below budget because the new equipment installed in Q1 experienced zero unplanned downtime. The Controller must identify whether the $87,000 net favorable variance represents genuine cost improvement or offsetting errors that require different management responses. Which analysis is most accurate?",
