    "Stem": "Castlebrook Industries' Q2 operating report shows a $154,000 unfavorable static budget variance (actual operating income of $392,000 vs. static budget of $546,000). The sales director claims this reflects the competitive environment and is outside management's control. The Controller prepares a flexible budget at actual volume (9,800 units vs. 12,000 budgeted) and finds: (a) Sales volume variance: $176,000 unfavorable — driven by the 2,200-unit shortfall at an $80 budgeted contribution margin per unit; (b) Flexible budget variance: $22,000 favorable — actual costs and revenues at 9,800 units were $22,000 better than the flexible budget predicted for that volume. The Controller must now interpret these findings for the monthly operating review. Which interpretation is most accurate?",
