    "Stem": "Deepwater Corporation's CEO has proposed replacing the company's current flexible-budget-based bonus system with static budget targets, arguing that 'managers should be held to the plan they committed to, not a moving target that adjusts downward when sales are weak.' The Controller analyzed the past three years and found: in Year 2, sales volume was 14% below the static budget due to a market downturn, but the flexible budget variance was $320,000 favorable — managers cut discretionary spending, renegotiated supplier contracts, and reduced overtime. Under the static budget, these managers would have received zero bonus despite saving the company $320,000. In Year 3, sales exceeded the static budget by 9% due to an unexpected competitor exit, producing a $185,000 favorable static budget variance, but the flexible budget variance was $74,000 unfavorable — managers increased spending proportionally with the volume surge. Under the static budget, they would have received full bonuses despite spending $74,000 more than the flexible budget standard. The board is divided. Which performance evaluation framework should the Controller recommend?",
