    "ExplanationWrongC": "Option C proposes phasing the automation over four years to avoid severance through attrition. This is financially clever — avoiding $236,772 in severance and giving the sales team time — but it misunderstands attrition dynamics. Welders who know their positions will be eliminated in Year 2 or Year 4 will not wait to be replaced; the most capable welders will leave immediately for stable employment elsewhere, leaving Ashfield with the least mobile workers during the transition. The attrition-based approach effectively selects for the lowest-performing welders while the highest-performing ones self-select out. Additionally, the company cannot control attrition timing — if only 2 welders leave in Year 1 instead of the assumed 4, the phase schedule is disrupted. A candidate selecting this option may have optimized the financial engineering of the transition without considering how workforce behavior responds to announced future layoffs.",
