    "ItemStyle": "single-select",
    "Stem": "Flagship Properties, a publicly traded REIT, appoints Dr. Harold Vance as chair of its audit committee. Dr. Vance holds a PhD in Real Estate Finance and an inactive CPA license that expired 18 years ago and was never renewed. He has spent his entire 32-year career in academia and real estate development, and has never prepared, audited, supervised the preparation of, or evaluated financial statements for a publicly traded company. The proxy statement filed with the SEC designates Dr. Vance as the audit committee's financial expert. A shareholder lawsuit alleges that this designation is materially misleading. Dr. Vance responds: 'I understand real estate finance at a doctoral level — that makes me more qualified than most financial experts who merely hold active licenses.' Evaluate whether Dr. Vance qualifies as an audit committee financial expert under COSO Principle 2 and SEC requirements.",
