    "ExplanationWrongB": "",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "Option C overstates COSO's requirements. COSO Principle 7 does not mandate purely quantitative methods such as VaR for all risks — it recognizes that risk assessment methodologies should be appropriate to the nature of the risk and the organization's capabilities. Many operational and strategic risks are appropriately assessed using qualitative or semi-quantitative methods. The deficiency at Northland was not that likelihood and impact ratings were used (they are legitimate risk assessment tools) but that the ratings were systematically biased. The remediation is to calibrate the qualitative ratings, not to eliminate them in favor of quantitative models that may themselves embed assumptions that introduce different biases.",
