    "Stem": "Meridian Capital Group, a mid-size asset manager subject to new SEC climate-related disclosure rules effective next fiscal year, maintains a COSO-aligned internal control framework. Meridian's existing risk assessment process categorizes risks into two buckets: \"Financial Risks\" (credit, market, liquidity) and \"Operational Risks\" (fraud, systems failure, business continuity). The board must determine whether the current risk assessment granularity is adequate under COSO Principle 7, given that the new regulations require entity-level disclosure of the firm's exposure to physical climate risks, transition risks, and the effectiveness of governance over climate-related matters — none of which are addressed by the current risk categories. Which recommendation is most consistent with COSO Principle 7?",
