    "Stem": "Pacific Rim Credit Union, a $4.1 billion financial institution, launched a mobile banking application that uses artificial intelligence to provide personalized financial advice to its 380,000 members. The AI model was developed by a third-party fintech vendor and was trained on aggregated member transaction data, credit scores, and demographic information. Six months after launch, the state banking regulator issued a cease-and-desist order, finding that the AI model systematically recommended higher-interest loan products to members in lower-income zip codes and investment products with higher fees to members over age 65, potentially violating fair lending and elder financial protection laws. Pacific Rim's risk register, last updated before the mobile app launch, did not include any risk related to AI model bias or algorithmic fairness. The Chief Risk Officer stated that 'model risk' was identified as a general category, but no specific AI-related risks had been assessed. Under COSO Principle 6, which of the following best evaluates Pacific Rim's risk identification?",
