    "Stem": "ValleyView Energy, a midstream oil and gas company, experienced three safety incidents in 18 months: a pipeline leak, a compressor station fire, and a chemical spill. After each incident, the CEO sent a company-wide email emphasizing that 'safety is our highest priority' and the board approved additional spending on safety equipment. However, an internal culture assessment conducted after the third incident revealed that: (1) operations managers who delayed maintenance to meet quarterly throughput targets received higher performance ratings than managers who missed targets due to safety-related downtime; (2) the risk committee met quarterly but had not changed its risk ratings for any operational risk in three years; (3) 67% of field employees surveyed said they 'would not report a near-miss because nothing changes after reporting'; and (4) safety incident investigations consistently identified 'operator error' as the root cause without examining systemic factors. Under COSO ERM, which of the following best evaluates ValleyView's risk culture?",
