    "Stem": "During a major restructuring at Atherton Industries, the Chief Restructuring Officer eliminated the internal audit director position as a cost savings measure, removing the primary communication channel between internal assurance functions and the audit committee. Controller Laura Nguyen subsequently identifies a material control deficiency in the newly consolidated accounts payable system — $847,000 in duplicate payments due to eliminated segregation of duties. Nguyen documents the deficiency and reports it to CFO David Hartwick with a recommendation to notify the audit committee. Hartwick decides not to escalate, reasoning that raising this now would delay the restructuring and embarrass the team before the board. Under COSO Principle 14, which of the following best evaluates the effectiveness of the control deficiency communication?",
