    "ItemType": "MCQ",
    "ItemStyle": "single-select",
    "Stem": "Velocity Manufacturing operates a just-in-time assembly system with 80% of raw materials arriving through a single container port. Velocity's risk identification process consists solely of an annual financial health review of each tier-1 supplier conducted by procurement. When a dockworker strike shut down the port and a critical tier-2 semiconductor supplier — which Velocity had never assessed — filed for bankruptcy in the same week, production halted for three weeks at a cost of $2.7 million in lost contribution margin. Which statement best evaluates the completeness of Velocity's risk identification under COSO Principle 6?",
